  "visualReviews": {
    "npc.civilian-man-a.aftermath": "Healthy Man A hair, teal shirt and khaki trouser identity remain comparable to the shipped peer. Forearm wrap reads at 135/190 px; chest dust is a broad dark gradient rather than surface grunge. LOD2 loses layered hair and sneaker detail but preserves the clothing blocks and wrap.",
    "npc.civilian-man-b.aftermath": "Cap, beard, mustard hoodie and dark jeans remain distinctly Man B at both sizes. Pale wrist wrap is visible; the dusty field is subtler than the reference wear. LOD2 omits hoodie cords and cap stitching; its clean closed cap silhouette is steadier than the shipped decimated far cap.",
    "npc.civilian-woman-b.aftermath": "Bun, glasses, lavender blouse, red lanyard and navy trousers match the shipped Woman B identity. Pale forearm wrap is less exposed from the fixed camera than from the opposite turntable view. LOD2 simplifies bun strands and bag trim while retaining glasses and the main clothing blocks. Fine soot is less visible at 135 px.",
    "npc.marcus.aftermath": "Teal/olive clothes, yellow organizer armband and pale left forearm wrap separate Marcus from the Man A peer at both sizes. Face and hair are the younger shipped Man A sculpt, unlike the older dark-shirt reference. LOD2 keeps the yellow band and pistol socket; shoe/hair detail is reduced.",
    "npc.shelter-survivor.bandaged": "Mustard clothing, large pale shoulder/forearm dressings, lowered head and bent elbow convey a living injured adult. Compared with the reference, there is no chest sling; dressings follow their rigid owners. LOD2 keeps the injury volumes, although the shoulder reads more angular and fingers become closed palms.",
    "npc.shelter-survivor.lying": "Whole body is visibly supine with head cushion and left arm folded back over the torso at 135/190 px. The upright signaling hand found in early QA was corrected and recaptured. Open healthy eyes convey resting rather than a corpse. Cushion is more rectangular than the reference; LOD2 retains reclined silhouette but shoes lose trim. Standing peer comparison makes the rest pose clear.",
    "npc.shelter-survivor.sitting": "Bent hips/knees and feet in front create an unmistakable mat-seated silhouette at both sizes. This is a low mat pose, not a bench-height pose. Arms extend slightly farther forward than the reference hands-on-knees posture. LOD2 keeps all bends, pale wrap and headband; hair and fingers simplify. Standing reset remains available."
  },
